From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:12:49 -0700
Subject: Harden XMLDocumentParserRs FFI borrows and re-entrancy handling

https://crrev.com/c/8602619 guarded XMLDocumentParserRs::ProcessEvents()
with in_process_events_ and pending_src_, but left several re-entrancy
and FFI borrowing issues:

1. xml_ffi::process_next_event() took &mut XmlReadState and held borrows
   into read_state.event_reader across C++ parser callbacks. Synchronous
   re-entry into xml_ffi from callbacks (such as DocType() calling
   add_xhtml_entities() or StartElementNs() and
   UpdateScriptStartPositionIfNeeded() calling GetTextPosition() ->
   try_get_last_event_position()) created aliasing &mut XmlReadState /
   &XmlReadState references across FFI (Rust undefined behavior) and
   mutated read_state.event_reader in add_xhtml_entities() while
   doctype_ids() still borrowed it.
2. Draining pending_src_ after the ProcessEvents() loop via a recursive
   Append() call caused the loop to hit a premature EOF on the prior
   chunk before feeding queued bytes and could duplicate pending_src_ in
   original_source_for_transform_.
3. The re-entrancy tests in xml_document_parser_sim_test.cc were not
   parameterized to run against both the libxml2 and Rust XML parsers,
   and did not cover re-entrant Append() calls when StartElementNs()
   flushes pending text via UpdateLeafTextNode().

Fix these issues by:
1. Using interior mutability (RefCell/Cell) in XmlReadState, passing
   &XmlReadState across FFI, and cloning the top declared Namespace
   entry and doctype strings in xml_ffi::process_next_event() before
   invoking parser_callbacks so read_state.event_reader is not borrowed
   across FFI callbacks.
2. Extracting XMLDocumentParserRs::AppendToSource() and draining
   pending_src_ inside the XMLDocumentParserRs::ProcessEvents() loop.
3. Parameterizing the re-entrancy tests in
   xml_document_parser_sim_test.cc to run against both the libxml2 and
   Rust XML parsers, and adding a test for re-entrant Append() during
   StartElementNs().

